Subject: [PATCH 2/7] relax: a fn body that defines a macro_rules! is parsed at
 load

body_outline deferred a body that defines a `macro_rules!` it does not call
(combine 4.6.7's tuple parsers: `#[allow(unused_macros)] macro_rules!
add_errors`, which the one-element tuple expands without a call). The lazy
parse then met an item and the load ended with "a lazily parsed fn body defined
an item (Relax bug; RELAX_LAZY_BODIES=0 works around it)".

A `macro_rules! name` in the body keeps it eager, as a call of an unknown macro
already did. The test runs the lazy package driver in a fresh loader, since
`relax test <file>` loads single files eagerly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
